# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
# NOTE: NO backticks and NO dollar-sign in the desc/blurb text below (shell-eval fragility -- see CLAUDE.md).
register_gate "tests/test_append_overlap.py" "APPEND OVERLAP GATE: PASS" "append overlap (overlapping appends are a real conflict, never softened)" "append overlap recall guard: the #356 append->serialize_soft demotion proves each side is a tail append past the file last symbol end-line (past_max), but past_max is PER SIDE -- it does NOT prove the two appends are disjoint FROM EACH OTHER. Two PRs that BOTH insert at the SAME tail line range (each past max, but their changed ranges OVERLAP) were wrongly graded relation 'append' -> serialize_soft, silently softening a REAL same-insertion-point textual conflict (the verdict ladder collision/serialize > warn > clear > unknown, so serialize_soft is a softened serialize = an under-warn). The fix adds NOT ranges_overlap to the 'append' arm of _file_pair_symbol_overlap: the two sides raw changed line ranges (claim.touched_ranges, the SAME content-free int4range data the finer mapping uses) must not overlap each other; when they do, the pair falls back to 'unknown' = HARD. Proven against the LIVE engine (main_impact_surface) on a constructed real extractor graph (content-free): NON-overlapping appends incl. a wide gap STAY serialize_soft (preserves #356, still visible) and the soft change is non-material; OVERLAPPING appends and SAME-insertion-point appends STAY HARD serialize and the hard change IS material (is_material_coupling True) so the pause tier may surface it. FAILS on origin/main where overlapping appends are wrongly softened." "append overlap fix: non-overlapping appends stay serialize_soft (neutral, #356 intent preserved); two appends whose line ranges OVERLAP each other (same insertion point) stay HARD serialize + material -- a real conflict is never silently softened" 18
